 els\nPinwheels\, serpentines\, and threadles\nProficient back sides and ju
 mp wraps\nNovice sends (6-10 ft gamble lines)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Specialty - Sports Sampler (Lea Pfeiffer)
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261011T153000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261011T163000Z
DTSTAMP;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261004T200405Z
UID:1791732600_Specialty-SportsSampler@luckydog
DESCRIPTION:Are you interested in dog sports but overwhelmed by the option
 s? This four-week class is a short introduction to tricks\, nosework\, agi
 lity\, and rally! We'll spend one week on the foundation skills for each s
 port so you can get a better idea of where your dog will really shine!
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Specialty - Zen Dog (Rachel Simmons)
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261011T153000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261011T162500Z
DTSTAMP;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261004T200405Z
UID:1791732600_Specialty-ZenDog@luckydog
DESCRIPTION:Does your dog have a hard time settling down in arousing situa
 tions\, such as when company is over or on restaurant patios? Do they get 
 nervous or display demand behaviors like barking\, whining\, or more when 
 you aren’t paying attention to them? If your dog is over-excited in new 
 situations or too nervous to calm down\, Zen Dog is the class for you! Fou
 r-weeks long\, this class will focus on teaching us how to nurture our dog
 s’ ability to self-soothe and settle in the home as well as in novel env
 ironments by incorporating impulse control\, the “art of doing nothing
 ” and more. These life-long skills can help set you and your dog up for 
 success at home or in public\, and are a great foundation for creating a h
 ealthier and more enjoyable relationship between you and your dog.\nIf thi
 s is your first class at Lucky Dog\, please attend an orientation before e
 nrolling.
END:VEVENT
