BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Specialty - Therapy Dog Prep/CGC (Rachel Simmons)
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261031T180000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261031T185500Z
DTSTAMP;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261004T200434Z
UID:1793469600_Specialty-TherapyDogPrep/CGC@luckydog
DESCRIPTION:Therapy Dog Prep and CGC\nWould you like to share your dog’s
  companionship with people in hospitals\, nursing homes\, schools\, or eve
 n in communities recovering from stressful situations or disasters? Therap
 y dogs provide comfort\, emotional support\, and affection in these settin
 gs.\nThe most important qualities of a therapy dog are temperament and sta
 bility. Is your dog friendly with both people and other dogs? Does your do
 g enjoy being petted and hugged by adults and children? How does your dog 
 respond to sudden loud noises or unexpected situations?\nIf your dog is ca
 lm\, gentle\, and enjoys interacting with others\, they may be an excellen
 t candidate for this therapy dog class.\nCanine Good Citizen\nThe CGC clas
 s is the first step to also becoming a Therapy Assistant Dog.  The 10 beh
 aviors that are learned in the CGC class will apply to the first 10 steps 
 in the Therapy test.  Therefore we combine the classes together so that w
 hatever your goals may be that you can accomplish that without having to t
 ake a separate class.\nThe AKC's Canine Good Citizen (CGC) program is reco
 gnized as the gold standard for dog behavior. Would you love for people to
  point at your dog and say\, I want my dog to act like that. That is what 
 we strive for in this class. We train for the 10 behaviors/commands that a
 re required for your dog to pass the Canine Good Citizen test.\nIf you wan
 t to know more about the CGC program\, click on this link\nhttp://www.akc.
 org/dog-owners/training/canine-good-citizen/what-is-canine-good-citizen/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Manners 3 - Advanced (Rachel Simmons)
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261101T151500Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261101T161000Z
DTSTAMP;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261004T200437Z
UID:1793546100_Manners3-Advanced@luckydog
DESCRIPTION:Ready to take your dog’s training to the next level? In Adva
 nced Manners\, we build on your basic foundation to add distractions\, lea
 ve treats behind\, and introduce some tricks to keep it interesting! This 
 class is designed to take your dog’s behavior above and beyond to make s
 ure he can keep his brain in any situation. If you want to get into therap
 y work\, dog sports\, or just want your best friend to go out and about wi
 th you\, Advanced Manners is the place to be!
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Canine Conditioning (Lea Pfeiffer)
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261101T151500Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261101T161000Z
DTSTAMP;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261004T200437Z
UID:1793546100_CanineConditioning@luckydog
DESCRIPTION:Canine Conditioning is a fun educational canine fitness class 
 designed to help dogs move with strength\, confidence\, and purpose.\nThro
 ugh safe\, low impact exercises\, dogs will improve their balance\, streng
 th\, flexibility\, coordination\, and body awareness while reducing their 
 risk of injury. Whether you have an athlete preparing for competition\, an
  adventure companion who loves hiking and exploring\, the daily running pa
 rtner\, or a senior dog who could benefit from gentle conditioning and imp
 rove mobility\, this class provides exercises that can be tailored to your
  dog’s individual needs.\nHandlers will also learn how to support their 
 dog’s long term health through proper warm ups and cool down routines\, 
 safe exercises\, and an understanding of how fitness contributes to overal
 l performance\, recovery\, and everyday wellness.\nCanine Conditioning is 
 about more than building stronger dogs-it’s about creating healthier mov
 ement for every stage of life.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Specialty - Sports Sampler (Lea Pfeiffer)
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261101T163000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261101T173000Z
DTSTAMP;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261004T200437Z
UID:1793550600_Specialty-SportsSampler@luckydog
DESCRIPTION:Are you interested in dog sports but overwhelmed by the option
 s? This four-week class is a short introduction to tricks\, nosework\, agi
 lity\, and rally! We'll spend one week on the foundation skills for each s
 port so you can get a better idea of where your dog will really shine!
END:VEVENT
